## What Support Does Not Buy

**No pay-to-remove listings.**

**No paid changes to evidence classifications.**

**No sponsor controls the findings.**

**No contribution changes the facts.**

**No organization receives favorable coverage because it funded the project.**

Corrections are made when stronger evidence establishes that the record is wrong, incomplete, or outdated.

That standard applies whether the correction helps or hurts the organization being documented.

## What We Stand For

We believe technical professionals deserve better than being handed accountability without authority.

We believe cybersecurity decisions should have identifiable ownership.

We believe risk should not disappear simply because it crossed a vendor boundary.

We believe technical warnings deserve a documented chain of escalation.

We believe executives and boards should understand the consequences of security decisions without scapegoating the engineers responsible for implementing them.

We believe bureaucracy should never become a substitute for security.

And we believe the public benefits when cyber incidents remain documented long enough for everyone else to learn from them.

